    <string name="timeline_help_chart">Battery % (left axis, blue) and memory available % (left axis, green) share the same 0–100 scale since both are percentages. Battery temperature (right axis, orange) is in °C. Pinch to zoom, drag to pan - the bands below stay in sync. Tap directly on the battery line for exact values at that point.</string>
    <string name="timeline_help_thermal">Android\'s thermal throttling status over time. Green = normal. Yellow/orange = light-to-moderate throttling. Red = severe or worse, meaning the OS is actively slowing the device down to cool it. Grey = unknown.</string>
    <string name="timeline_help_doze">Yellow = screen on. Light blue = Doze (deep idle, most background work paused). Grey = screen off but not yet dozing. Screen-on is drawn on top of the Doze color, so a yellow stretch always means the screen was actually on.</string>
    <string name="timeline_help_sessions">Each color block is one app in the foreground; width is how long it stayed there. Colors are assigned in the order apps first appear in this range, not by app identity - the same app can get a different color in a different range.</string>
